{"type": "message", "id": "ea74e308", "parentId": "6235c9fa", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T11:18:15.273Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_5u9Ua2Bb6yWRACYncOXIukv8", "toolName": "exec", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "xrdb: Can't open display ''\n/root/.bashrc: line 16: bind: warning: line editing not enabled\nKY -> https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\n--- /tmp/KY8.txt ---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT\nKENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n\nOVERALL RESULTS\n• In 2022, the average score of eighth-grade students in Kentucky was 269. This was\nlower than the average score of 273 for students in the nation.\n• The average score for students in Kentucky in 2022 (269) was lower than their\naverage score in 2019 (278) and was not significantly different from their average\nscore in 2000 (270).\n• The percentage of students in Kentucky who performed at or above the NAEP\nProficient level was 21 percent in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019\n(29 percent) and was not significantly different from that in 2000 (20 percent).\n• The percentage of students in Kentucky who performed at or above the NAEP Basic\nlevel was 57 percent in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (67\npercent) and was not significantly different from that in 2000 (60 percent).\n\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\nRESULTS\nKentucky\n\nAverage Score\n\n2000\n\n40\n\n40*\n\n18\n\n2019\n\n33*\n\n38\n\n22*\n\n2022\n\n43\n\n35\n\n17\n\n40*\n\n35\n\n19\n\n3\n\n270\n7*\n\n278*\n\n4\n\n269\n\nNation (public)\n2022\n\nPercent below NAEP Basic\nor at NAEP Basic level\nBelow NAEP Basic\n\nNAEP Basic\n\n7*\n\n273*\n\nPercent at NAEP Proficient\nor NAEP Advanced level\n\nNAEP Proficient\n\nNAEP Advanced\n\nGraph\n270\n278,\n269\n273,\nscore\nAverage\n3\n4\n7,\nAdvanced\n18\n22,\n17\n19.\nProficient\n38\n35\n35.\nat\n40\n2000\n33,\n2019\n43\nIn\nKentucky\n2022.\nresults\nstate's\nfrom\ndifferent\nsignificantly\n40,\n=\n2022\nlevel\nBasic\nNAEP\nbelow\nscoring\nNation\nthe\nin\nstudents\nof\nPercent\ndetails:\n* Significantly different (p < .05) from the state's results in 2022. Significance tests were performed\nusing unrounded numbers.\nNOTE: NAEP achievement levels are to be used on a trial basis and should be interpreted and used\nwith caution. Detail may not sum to totals because of rounding.\n\nCOMPARE THE AVERAGE SCORE IN 2022 TO OTHER STATES/\nJURISDICTIONS\n\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC)\nScore\n500\n\nAK\n\nME\nVT\nWA\n\nMT\n\nND\n\nMN\n\nWI\n\nMI\n\nNY\n\nNH\nMA\n\n290\nRI\n\n281*\nID\nOR\n\nWY\nNV\n\nCA\n\nSD\nCO\n\nAZ\n\nIA\nNE\n\nUT\nNM\n\nIL\nMO\n\nKS\nOK\n\nIN\nKY\n\nAR\nLA\n\nOH\nKS -> https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf\n--- /tmp/KS8.txt ---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT\nKANSAS  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n\nOVERALL RESULTS\n• In 2022, the average score of eighth-grade students in Kansas was 272. This was not\nsignificantly different from the average score of 273 for students in the nation.\n• The average score for students in Kansas in 2022 (272) was lower than their average\nscore in 2019 (282) and in 2000 (283).\n• The percentage of students in Kansas who performed at or above the NAEP Proficient\nlevel was 23 percent in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (33\npercent) and in 2000 (34 percent).\n• The percentage of students in Kansas who performed at or above the NAEP Basic\nlevel was 61 percent in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (71\npercent) and in 2000 (76 percent).\n\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\nRESULTS\nKansas\n\nAverage Score\n\n2000\n\n24*\n\n2019\n\n43*\n\n29*\n\n2022\n\n29*\n\n5\n\n283*\n\n38\n\n24*\n\n9*\n\n282*\n\n39\n\n37\n\n18\n\n5\n\n272\n\n40\n\n35\n\n19\n\n7*\n\n273\n\nNation (public)\n2022\n\nPercent below NAEP Basic\nor at NAEP Basic level\nBelow NAEP Basic\n